      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Plan maintenance, inspections and compliance activities.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 48703,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, I've created an initial proposal for the portfolio-wide Maintenance and Inspection Master Schedule, which you can find in A5. This is the first step for T6. I'd like to get your input, especially from @167424 on the practicalities.",
            "mentions": [
              167424
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "T6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 167424,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "Thanks @48703. I've reviewed A5. The proposed annual checks for HVAC and fire safety systems are good. For the older South Heights building, I'd suggest bi-annual plumbing inspections. We've had a few minor leaks there, and preventive checks would be cheaper than repairs. The data from T5 inventory supports this.",
            "mentions": [
              48703
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "wrench",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 48703,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "Excellent point. That's exactly the kind of on-the-ground insight we need. I'll update A5 to include bi-annual plumbing inspections for all pre-1980 buildings. This brings us to the decision on inspection frequency. Any other thoughts on this?",
            "mentions": [
              167424
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 128593,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "Just to confirm, will the schedule align with the notice periods required in our rental agreements? We need to ensure we give tenants adequate warning for non-emergency inspections.",
            "mentions": [
              48703
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 48703,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "Yes, absolutely. The scheduling process in A5 will have a built-in lead time for tenant notifications, which will be based on the templates from T9.",
            "mentions": [
              128593
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 48703,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "Hearing no other comments, let's formalize this. We'll set inspection frequencies based on building age and system type as detailed in the updated A5. This includes annual checks for core systems and bi-annual for specific risks in older buildings.",
            "mentions": [
              54175
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 54175,
            "reply_to": "M30",
            "text": "Approved.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 48703,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "Great. Now for compliance. @167424, you've been working on the health, safety, and energy checklist for T12. Can you share the key items we need to make mandatory for all buildings?",
            "mentions": [
              167424
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 167424,
            "reply_to": "M32",
            "text": "Of course. I've documented the draft checklist for T12. The mandatory items should be: fire extinguisher checks, smoke detector tests, clear emergency exit paths, and annual energy performance certificate validation. These cover our main legal requirements.",
            "mentions": [
              48703
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 48703,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "That sounds comprehensive and covers the critical risks. I agree these should be mandatory. Any objections to confirming these items for the compliance checklist?",
            "mentions": [
              54175,
              128593
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 128593,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Looks good to me. It aligns with standard compliance practices.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 54175,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Confirm.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 48703,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "Excellent. Decision D6 is confirmed. The compliance checklist items in T12 are mandatory. @167424, please finalize that document and upload it. I will integrate it into the master schedule A5.",
            "mentions": [
              167424
            ],
